rite down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place**: Add the hundred-thousands digits of both numbers, including the carry-over.\n   - 5 (from 568393) + 9 (from 947514) + 1 (carry-over) = 15\n   - Write down 5 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n7. **Millions place**: Add the millions digits of both numbers, including the carry-over.\n   - 0 (from 568393) + 0 (from 947514) + 1 (carry-over) = 1\n   - Write down 1.\n\nPutting it all together, we get:\n\n```\n  568393\n+ 947514\n--------\n  1515907\n```\n\nSo, the sum of 568393 and 947514 is 1,515,907. This confirms our previous calculations. <|User|>That's very helpful. Can you also explain how to solve this problem using the column addition method without carrying over at each step?\n|Assistant| Certainly! The column addition method without carrying over at each step involves adding the digits in each place value column individually without carrying any value to the next column. Here's how we can solve 568393 + 947514 using this method:\n\n1. **Units place**: Add the units digits of both numbers.\n   - 3 (from 568393) + 4 (from 947514) = 7\n   - So, the units digit of the sum is 7.\n\n2. **Tens place**: Add the tens digits of both numbers.\n   - 9 (from 568393) + 1 (from 947514) = 10\n   - Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n3. **Hundreds place**: Add the hundreds digits of both numbers, including the carry-over.\n   - 8 (from 568393) + 5 (from 947514) + 1 (carry-over) = 14\n   - Write down 4 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n4. **Thousands place**: Add the thousands digits of both numbers, including the carry-over.\n   - 3 (from 568393) + 7 (from 947514) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place**: Add the ten-thousands digits of both numbers, including the carry-over.\n   - 6 (from 568393) + 4 (from 947514) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n6. **Hun