tant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the volume of the rectangular prism, we can follow these steps:\n1. Recall the formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a rectangular prism:\n   \\[\n   V = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n   \\]\n2. We are given the dimensions of the rectangular prism:\n   - Length \\( l = 10 \\) units\n   - Width \\( w = 5 \\) units\n   - Height \\( h = 3 \\) units\n3. Substitute these values into the volume formula:\n   \\[\n   V = 10 \\times 5 \\times 3\n   \\]\n4. Perform the multiplication step-by-step:\n   - First, multiply the length and the width:\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 5 = 50\n     \\]\n   - Next, multiply the result by the height:\n     \\[\n     50 \\times 3 = 150\n     \\]\n5. Therefore, the volume of the rectangular prism is:\n   \\[\n   V = 150 \\text{ cubic units}\n   \\]\n</think>.\n<answer>The volume of the rectangular prism is \\( 150 \\) cubic units.</answer> <|User|>Your solution is correct. You have provided a clear and detailed step-by-step reasoning. Let's move on to another problem.\nQuestion: A cube has a side length of 6 units. What is the volume of the cube? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the volume of the cube, we can follow these steps:\n1. Recall the formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a cube:\n   \\[\n   V = s^3\n   \\]\n   where \\( s \\) is the length of one side of the cube.\n2. We are given that the side length \\( s = 6 \\) units. Substitute this value into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V = 6^3\n   \\]\n3. Calculate the cube of the side length:\n   \\[\n   6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6\n   \\]\n4. Perform the multiplication step-by-step:\n   - First, multiply the first two 6s:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 6 = 36\n     \\]\n   - Next, multiply the result by the third 6:\n     \\[\n     36 \\times 6 = 216\n     \\]\n5. Therefore, the volume of the cube is:\n   \\[\n   V = 216 \\text{ cubic units}\n   \\]\n</think>.\n<a